            "field_project_story_body": [
                {
                    "value": "<h2>No Man\u2019s Sky and the element cards</h2>\r\nWhen I first saw the inventory management in No Man\u2019s Sky, I was immediately fascinated by the cards for its individual elements. My first reaction was that this was one of the best things I had ever seen in a game interface. It set me thinking about what I could do with that idea in my own incremental game.\r\n\r\nI wanted to use that sense of discovery to help players learn about real chemical elements, atoms, molecules and subatomic particles. The cards could become a way to explore and understand matter through play. This was one of the starting points for SMEP, and the idea has continued to evolve as I have worked on the project.",
                    "format": "full_html"
                }
            ]
        },
